      "latin": "ēmittō, ēmittere, ēmīsī, ēmissum",
      "status": "recommended",
      "period": "modern",
      "gloss": "broadcast (on radio or television)",
      "evidence": [
        "Traupman 283"
      ],
      "comment": "Classically to send out, let go, and also to publish a book (Cic. Fam. 7.33; Suet. Claud. 33); the broadcasting sense is modern. The noun, a broadcast, is <span lang=\"la\">ēmissiō, ēmissiōnis f.</span> (Traupman 283)."
    },
    {
      "latin": "per aetheris undās dīmittō",
      "status": "alternative",
      "period": "modern",
      "gloss": "send out over the airwaves",
      "evidence": [
        "M-O s.v. broadcast (Egger)"
      ],
      "comment": "A fuller phrase; Morgan–Owens also gives <span lang=\"la\">ēmittere</span> and <span lang=\"la\">dīvulgāre</span> with it."
    },
    {
      "latin": "dīvulgō, dīvulgāre, dīvulgāvī, dīvulgātum",
      "status": "alternative",
      "period": "classical",
      "gloss": "spread abroad, make widely known",
      "comment": "The classical word for making news public; not of the technical act of broadcasting."
    },
